Revela's plugin system lets you extend your site with additional features. Official plugins are distributed as **NuGet packages** (`.nupkg`) attached to each [GitHub Release](https://github.com/Spectara/Revela/releases). They are not published on NuGet.org yet.

<div class="features-grid">

### 📦 Compression

Pre-compress HTML, CSS, and JS with Gzip and Brotli for 70-95% smaller files.

### 📊 Statistics

Analyze EXIF data from your photos – cameras, lenses, apertures, ISO, and timeline.

### 🌐 Dev Server

Preview your generated site locally during development.

### ☁️ OneDrive Source

Sync photos from OneDrive shared folders directly into your project.

</div>

## Official Plugins

| Plugin | Package | Description |
|--------|---------|-------------|
| **Compression** | `Spectara.Revela.Plugins.Compress` | Pre-compress static files with Gzip and Brotli |
| **Statistics** | `Spectara.Revela.Plugins.Statistics` | Generate EXIF statistics pages |
| **Serve** | `Spectara.Revela.Plugins.Serve` | Local development server |
| **OneDrive** | `Spectara.Revela.Plugins.Source.OneDrive` | Download photos from OneDrive shared folders |
| **Calendar** | `Spectara.Revela.Plugins.Calendar` | Availability calendar (booked/free days) from iCal `.ics` files |
| **Source.Calendar** | `Spectara.Revela.Plugins.Source.Calendar` | Download iCal feeds (e.g. booking exports) into the source folder |

All `Spectara.Revela.*` release packages come with a `SHA256SUMS` file and Sigstore (cosign) signatures on the GitHub Release.

## Installing Plugins

How you get plugins depends on your edition:

- **Standalone**: all official plugins are built in. There is nothing to install, and the `plugin` commands are not available.
- **Full**: the `packages/` folder next to the executable is used as a local feed (`bundled`), so the commands below work offline.
- **.NET tool**: there is no bundled folder. Download the `.nupkg` files from the release into a folder and register it once with `revela config feed add releases /absolute/path/to/folder`.

```bash
# Install by short name
revela plugin install Statistics

# Or use full package ID
revela plugin install Spectara.Revela.Plugins.Statistics

# Install a specific version
revela plugin install Statistics --version 1.2.0
```

## Managing Plugins

```bash
# List installed plugins
revela plugin list

# Remove a plugin
revela plugin uninstall Statistics
```

## Configuration

Plugins store their settings in `project.json` below `plugins`, each under its own key (`serve`, `statistics`, `oneDrive`, `calendarFeeds`):

```json
{
  "plugins": {
    "statistics": {
      "maxEntriesPerCategory": 15,
      "sortByCount": true
    },
    "serve": {
      "port": 8080
    }
  }
}
```

Settings can also be overridden with environment variables (`SPECTARA__REVELA__PLUGINS__<KEY>__<SETTING>`):

```bash
SPECTARA__REVELA__PLUGINS__SERVE__PORT=3000
```

## Community Plugins

Revela supports third-party plugins from any NuGet source. Community plugins use their own package prefix:

```bash
# Install from custom NuGet feed
revela plugin install MyPlugin --source https://my-feed.example.com/v3/index.json
```

> **Note:** Community plugins are not verified by Spectara. Install at your own risk.

## Restoring Dependencies

After cloning a project, updating Revela, or sharing your project with someone else, use `restore` to install all required themes and plugins:

```bash
# Install missing themes and plugins
revela restore

# Check only (don't install)
revela restore --check
```

Revela reads the `theme`, `themes`, and `plugins` sections from your configuration and installs anything that's missing.
